 "intro": "Mount Vesuvius, Campania, 73 BC. Seventy gladiators led by the Thracian Spartacus have escaped from a training school at Capua and taken refuge on the mountain. You are the praetor Gaius Claudius Glaber, with 3,000 militia.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s and Frontinus’s accounts, Glaber blocked the only path down from the summit, expecting the gladiators to starve. They made ladders from wild vines, climbed down the cliffs at night and fell on his camp from behind; the militia fled. Slaves and herdsmen flocked to Spartacus, who defeated several Roman armies over the next two years. The other choices are what-ifs.",
